<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n114419" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χορ-ευτής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οῦ</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>choral dancer,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				12.27
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				443
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				373b
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν χ. ἐξάγειν τινά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					And.
					4.20
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ἐπινίκια ἔθυεν αὐτός τε καὶ οἱ
					χ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Smp.</u>
					173a
				</span></i>
			: metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[θεοῦ] χ.</span>
			<i>the devoted follower</i> of a god, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Phdr.</u>
				252d
			</span></i>; of a philosopher, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ Πυθαγόρου καὶ Πλάτωνος καὶ
					Ἀριστοτέλους χ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Jul.
					<u>Or.</u>
					6.197d
				</span></i>
			: generally, <i>pupil,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Lib.
				<u>Or.</u>
				54.38
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> epith. of
			Pan, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				99
			</span></i>; of Dionysus, <i><span class="en">
				Orph.
			</span></i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Εὐχή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					9
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> used of
			dolphins, from their movements, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Anacreont.</u>
				55.24
			</span></i>; of cicadae, <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				1.20
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
